
# Builing A SQLite Test Dataset

There are several components to a testing dataset.  The following steps should
be executed in order, and assume the working directory is
`$EST_HOME/tests/test_data/small_data`.  The datasets are based on the Pfam
family PF07476.

## Step 0: Directory structure

    EST_HOME=/path/to/EST/repository
    EFI_FULL_DB=/path/to/EFI/blast/database/combined.fasta
    helper_dir=$EST_HOME/pipelines/buildefi/test_dataset
    data_dir=$EST_HOME/tests/test_data/smalldata
    mkdir -p $data_dir/work
    cd $data_dir
    EFI_DB_NAME=...
    EFI_DB_HOST=...
    

## Step 1: SQLite-based EFI database

SQLite-based datasets are best used for installation testing.  Assuming that the
helper scripts are located in `$EST_HOME/pipelines/buildefi/test_dataset`, use
the following recipe to build one from an existing EFI MySQL database:

    cat $helper_dir/get_subset_data.sql | mysql -N -h $EFI_DB_HOST -p $EFI_DB_NAME > work/raw_data
    perl $helper_dir/split_raw_data.pl < work/raw_data > import_data.sql
    
    awk -f $helper_dir/mysql2sqlite $helper_dir/efi_db_schema.sql | sqlite3 efi_db.sqlite
    
    sqlite3 efi_db.sqlite < import_data.sql


## Step 2: Config and ID files

    echo 'PF07476' > family_id.txt
    echo -e '[database]\ndbi=sqlite\n' > efi.config
    cut -f2 work/PFAM.tab > accession_test.txt
    echo -e 'node_label\tcluster_num_by_seq\tcluster_num_by_node' > gnd_id_list.txt
    cat accession_test.txt >> gnd_id_list.txt

    echo 'SELECT annotations.accession FROM annotations LEFT JOIN PFAM ON PFAM.accession = annotations.accession WHERE annotations.is_fragment = 0 AND PFAM.id = "PF07476"' | sqlite3 efi_db.sqlite > work/complete_ids.txt
    echo 'SELECT DISTINCT uniref90_seed FROM uniref LEFT JOIN PFAM ON PFAM.accession = uniref.accession WHERE PFAM.id = "PF07476"' | sqlite3 efi_db.sqlite > work/uniref90_ids.txt
    echo 'SELECT DISTINCT uniref90_seed FROM uniref LEFT JOIN PFAM ON PFAM.accession = uniref.accession LEFT JOIN annotations ON annotations.accession = uniref.accession WHERE PFAM.id = "PF07476" AND annotations.is_fragment = 0' | sqlite3 efi_db.sqlite > work/uniref90_complete_ids.txt
    echo 'SELECT DISTINCT uniref50_seed FROM uniref LEFT JOIN PFAM ON PFAM.accession = uniref.accession WHERE PFAM.id = "PF07476"' | sqlite3 efi_db.sqlite > work/uniref50_ids.txt
    echo 'SELECT DISTINCT uniref50_seed FROM uniref LEFT JOIN PFAM ON PFAM.accession = uniref.accession LEFT JOIN annotations ON annotations.accession = uniref.accession WHERE PFAM.id = "PF07476" AND annotations.is_fragment = 0' | sqlite3 efi_db.sqlite > work/uniref50_complete_ids.txt


## Step 3: FASTA retrieval

The master EFI BLAST sequence database is required for retrieving the sample
dataset sequences.  The following steps assume that the location of this
database is at `$EFI_FULL_DB`.  Additionally, legacy BLAST must be installed.

### BLAST installation

Most systems contain recent versions of BLAST.  The EFI tools use the legacy
version (2.2.26) of BLAST.  If legacy BLAST is installed on the system, then
set the `$fasta_cmd` and `$formatdb_cmd` variables:

    fastacmd_cmd="fastacmd"
    formatdb_cmd="formatdb"

If BLAST 2.2.26 is not available, then it must be installed using the
following steps:

    curl -o blast.tar.gz https://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/blast/executables/legacy.NOTSUPPORTED/2.2.26/blast-2.2.26-x64-linux.tar.gz
    tar zxvf blast.tar.gz
    fastacmd_cmd="$PWD/blast-2.2.26/bin/fastacmd"
    formatdb_cmd="$PWD/blast-2.2.26/bin/formatdb"

### BLAST database creation

    mkdir -p blastdb
    rm blastdb/*
    $fastacmd_cmd -d $EFI_FULL_DB -i accession_test.txt -o fasta_test.fasta
    $fastacmd_cmd -d $EFI_FULL_DB -i work/complete_ids.txt -o blastdb/combined_nr.fasta
    $fastacmd_cmd -d $EFI_FULL_DB -i work/uniref90_ids.txt -o blastdb/uniref90.fasta
    $fastacmd_cmd -d $EFI_FULL_DB -i work/uniref90_complete_ids.txt -o blastdb/uniref90_nr.fasta
    $fastacmd_cmd -d $EFI_FULL_DB -i work/uniref50_ids.txt -o blastdb/uniref50.fasta
    $fastacmd_cmd -d $EFI_FULL_DB -i work/uniref50_complete_ids.txt -o blastdb/uniref50_nr.fasta
    
    seq_id=$(head -1 accession_test.txt)
    $fastacmd_cmd -d $EFI_FULL_DB -o blast_query.fa -s $seq_id
    
    cp fasta_test.fasta blastdb/combined.fasta
    cd blastdb
    $formatdb_cmd -i combined.fasta -p T -o T
    $formatdb_cmd -i combined_nr.fasta -p T -o T
    $formatdb_cmd -i uniref90.fasta -p T -o T
    $formatdb_cmd -i uniref90_nr.fasta -p T -o T
    $formatdb_cmd -i uniref50.fasta -p T -o T
    $formatdb_cmd -i uniref50_nr.fasta -p T -o T
    cd ..


## Step 4: DIAMOND database

The CGFP tools use DIAMOND, so DIAMOND databases should be created as follows:

    mkdir -p diamonddb
    diamond makedb --in blastdb/combined.fasta -d diamonddb/combined.fasta
    diamond makedb --in blastdb/combined_nr.fasta -d diamonddb/combined_nr.fasta
    diamond makedb --in blastdb/uniref90.fasta -d diamonddb/uniref90.fasta
    diamond makedb --in blastdb/uniref90_nr.fasta -d diamonddb/uniref90_nr.fasta
    diamond makedb --in blastdb/uniref50.fasta -d diamonddb/uniref50.fasta
    diamond makedb --in blastdb/uniref50_nr.fasta -d diamonddb/uniref50_nr.fasta


## Step 5: Cleanup

    rm -rf work
    rm import_data.sql


# SSN files

SSN files should be generated with the official EFI-EST tools using the Family option
with PF07476 as the family.  Three jobs should be created: UniProt, UniRef90, 
and UniRef50.  Two files should be downloaded from the UniProt job: a full SSN and
a 70% repnode SSN.  The full SSN from both UniRef jobs should be downloaded.  These
should be placed in the test dataset directory and named as follows:

    ssn.xgmml.zip (compressed UniProt)
    ssn_repnode70.xgmml.zip (compressed 70% repnode UniProt)
    ssn_uniref90.xgmml.zip (compressed UniRef90)
    ssn_uniref50.xgmml (uncompressed UniRef50)


# Building A MySQL Dataset

Step 0 is followed for both SQLite and MySQL dataset build processes.  Steps 1 and 2
in the SQLite dataset build process are replaced with a single step, detailed below.
This configuration assumes that the MySQL server will be accessible by the testing
scripts.  After performing Step 1, follow Steps 3-5 in the SQLite dataset build
process.

## Step 1: Config and ID files

    echo 'PF07476' > family_id.txt
    if [[ ! -e "efi.config" ]]; then
        # This string should be edited to replace USER, PASSWORD, HOST, and PORT with the
        # relevant values
        echo -e '[database]\nuser=$USER\npassword=$PASSWORD\nhost=$HOST\nport=$PORT\ndbi=mariadb\n' > efi.config
        echo 'Configure efi.config before running tests'
    fi
    
    # This string should be edited to the relevant value
    EFI_DB_NAME=efi_db
    echo 'SELECT accession FROM PFAM WHERE id = "PF07476"' | mysql -N -h $HOST -p $EFI_DB_NAME > accession_test.txt
    echo -e 'node_label\tcluster_num_by_seq\tcluster_num_by_node' > gnd_id_list.txt
    cat accession_test.txt >> gnd_id_list.txt

    echo 'SELECT annotations.accession FROM annotations LEFT JOIN PFAM ON PFAM.accession = annotations.accession WHERE annotations.is_fragment = 0 AND PFAM.id = "PF07476"' | mysql -N -h $HOST -p $EFI_DB_NAME > work/complete_ids.txt
    echo 'SELECT DISTINCT uniref90_seed FROM uniref LEFT JOIN PFAM ON PFAM.accession = uniref.accession WHERE PFAM.id = "PF07476"' | mysql -N -h $HOST -p $EFI_DB_NAME > work/uniref90_ids.txt
    echo 'SELECT DISTINCT uniref90_seed FROM uniref LEFT JOIN PFAM ON PFAM.accession = uniref.accession LEFT JOIN annotations ON annotations.accession = uniref.accession WHERE PFAM.id = "PF07476" AND annotations.is_fragment = 0' | mysql -N -h $HOST -p $EFI_DB_NAME > work/uniref90_complete_ids.txt
    echo 'SELECT DISTINCT uniref50_seed FROM uniref LEFT JOIN PFAM ON PFAM.accession = uniref.accession WHERE PFAM.id = "PF07476"' | mysql -N -h $HOST -p $EFI_DB_NAME > work/uniref50_ids.txt
    echo 'SELECT DISTINCT uniref50_seed FROM uniref LEFT JOIN PFAM ON PFAM.accession = uniref.accession LEFT JOIN annotations ON annotations.accession = uniref.accession WHERE PFAM.id = "PF07476" AND annotations.is_fragment = 0' | mysql -N -h $HOST -p $EFI_DB_NAME > work/uniref50_complete_ids.txt

